# 1. Backend Design

The backend is structured using a layered architecture to ensure maintainability, separation of concerns, and scalability.

## Project Structure

```text
app/
├── routers/        # API endpoints only
├── services/       # Business logic layer
├── models/         # SQLAlchemy ORM models
├── schemas/        # Pydantic request/response validation
├── middleware/     # JWT auth, logging, rate limiting
├── dependencies/   # RBAC logic
├── exceptions/     # Global exception handling
├── database.py     # Async database engine and session
└── main.py         # App initialization and middleware registration
```

## Design Decisions

* Routers are intentionally thin and only handle HTTP transport.
* Business logic is fully isolated inside the `services/` layer.
* Services contain zero FastAPI imports, making them independently testable.
* Authentication, RBAC, logging, and rate limiting are extracted into middleware and reusable dependencies.
* API routes are versioned using `/api/v1/...`.

This structure ensures the application remains easy to extend, debug, and maintain.

